event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_08b2f514691c0c8f016aa3e5c73f7487d28f1581baff4e63f2","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":6458,"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Transaction Batch Boundary\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract derived from CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C, their supplied\n    copybooks and batch dependencies. The three operations invoke individual\n    program capabilities, not the complete JCL schedule.\n\n    HTTP POST, JSON envelopes, dataset binding identifiers, inline sequential\n    records and returned artifacts are chosen transport conventions. They are\n    not interfaces implemented by the COBOL source. A dataset binding identifies\n    an environment-provisioned file with the specified organization, keys and\n    access permissions; it does not create, validate, back up or repair that file.\n    Missing records and unavailable bindings remain representable failure inputs.\n\n    Structured character fields are right-padded with spaces to their PIC X\n    widths. Numeric identifier strings retain leading zeros. Decimal strings\n    encode signed fixed-point values, not floating-point numbers. Raw records\n    provide a lossless alternative, including filler and invalid numeric storage.\n    Raw record encoding and signed DISPLAY representation depend on the bound\n    COBOL runtime. No calendar, card-number, positive-amount, active-account or\n    reference-code validation is added by this contract.\n\n    Program completion, business rejection and abnormal termination are distinct.\n    HTTP 200 denotes a completed invocation, including posting with rejects.\n    HTTP 500 denotes an observed runtime failure or requested abnormal termination,\n    not a transactional rollback. No atomicity, retry, idempotency or automatic\n    recovery is promised. Artifacts and persistent changes may precede failure.\n  license:\n    name: Apache License 2.0\n    identifier: Apache-2.0\nx-uncertainties:\n  - |\n    The supplied JCL references SORT, IDCAMS and CEE3ABD; their implementations\n    and execution in the target environment are not established. REPROC also\n    references CNTLLIB(REPROCT), whose contents are not supplied.\n  - |\n    TRANBKP describes unloading, deleting and redefining the transaction master.\n    COMBTRAN describes sorting a backup plus system transactions by transaction\n    ID and loading the master. Neither is performed implicitly by these operations.\n  - |\n    TRANREPT JCL describes unloading, date filtering and sorting by card number\n    before CBTRN03C. The program operation does not assume those steps run.\n    Its SORT dates are separate from DATEPARM and its JCL has duplicate STEP05R\n    names. No schedule validity or equivalence of date sources is guaranteed.\n  - |\n    Numeric overflow has no explicit ON SIZE ERROR handling. Several working\n    totals use S9(09)V99 even though account balances use S9(10)V99. Runtime\n    behavior for overflow, invalid numeric bytes and unspecified initial storage\n    is not normalized by this contract.\npaths:\n  /transaction-postings:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Post an ordered daily transaction stream\n      description: |\n        Runs CBTRN02C. Opens DALYTRAN INPUT, TRANFILE OUTPUT (indexed,\n        random access, transaction ID key), XREFFILE INPUT, DALYREJS OUTPUT,\n        ACCTFILE I-O and TCATBALF I-O. The source does not open TRANFILE\n        EXTEND or I-O; this is not an append-to-history guarantee. Provisioning\n        and OPEN OUTPUT behavior of an existing indexed file are runtime\n        preconditions, not a hidden backup/reload workflow.\n\n        Each successfully read daily record increments the processed count.\n        Card lookup precedes account lookup. INVALID KEY on card lookup rejects\n        with 0100, \"INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\". INVALID KEY on account lookup\n        rejects with 0101, \"ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\". For a found account,\n        temporary balance is currentCycleCredit - currentCycleDebit + amount\n        in S9(09)V99. A value greater than creditLimit sets 0102,\n        \"OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\". Then expirationDate is compared as PIC X(10)\n        against the first ten characters of originalTimestamp. An earlier\n        expiration sets 0103, \"TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\",\n        overwriting 0102 if both apply. Equality passes both tests.\n        These lookups do not generally check all file statuses.\n\n        A rejected record writes the unchanged 350-byte input plus a four-digit\n        reason and a space-padded 76-character description. It does not enter\n        posting. Processing continues. A completed run with any rejects explicitly\n        sets COBOL RETURN-CODE to 4; no explicit zero assignment is made for a\n        reject-free run.\n\n        For a validated record, named transaction fields are copied, except\n        processingTimestamp is replaced by CURRENT-DATE in\n        YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 form. Input processingTimestamp is not used\n        for validation or posting. Output filler is not explicitly copied.\n\n        Persistent effects occur in this order:\n        1. Read category balance by account ID, type and category; status 23\n           creates an initialized record with balance equal to amount, otherwise\n           add amount and rewrite.\n        2. Add amount to account currentBalance. For amount >= 0 add amount to\n           currentCycleCredit; for negative amount add the negative amount to\n           currentCycleDebit. Rewrite the account.\n        3. Write the transaction keyed by its supplied ID.\n\n        Account rewrite INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109,\n        \"ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\", but the caller does not revisit rejection,\n        count it as rejected or write a reject record; transaction writing still\n        follows. Other account rewrite statuses are not explicitly checked.\n        Duplicate transaction IDs are not prevalidated or deduplicated. A\n        duplicate-key write failure takes the abnormal path after preceding\n        balance effects. Processing preserves input order; later records can\n        observe earlier changes.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Indexed master files must be provisioned and accessible in the declared modes.\n        - XREFFILE is keyed by card number; ACCTFILE by account ID; TCATBALF by account ID, type and category.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [dailyTransactions, transactionFile, crossReferenceFile, accountFile, categoryBalanceFile]\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  type: array\n                  description: DALYTRAN records in read order; empty input is allowed. IDs need not be unique.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                transactionFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed, possibly with business rejects and COBOL return code 4.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/AbnormalExecution'\n  /interest-transactions:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate sequential system interest transactions from category balances\n      description: |\n        Runs CBACT04C. Opens TCATBALF INPUT for sequential indexed-key traversal,\n        XREFFILE INPUT with account-ID alternate-key lookup, DISCGRP INPUT,\n        ACCTFILE I-O, and TRANSACT OUTPUT as a new sequential artifact.\n\n        On each account change, except the first, rewrite the previous account:\n        add accumulated monthly interest to currentBalance and set both cycle\n        credit and debit to zero. Then reset the accumulated interest, read the\n        new account and read its cross reference by account ID. Missing account\n        or cross reference is abnormal termination, not a skipped account.\n\n        For each category balance, look up disclosure rate by account group,\n        transaction type and category. Status 23 retries the lookup using the\n        space-padded group \"DEFAULT\" and the same type/category. Failure of this\n        default lookup is abnormal termination. A zero rate generates nothing.\n        Every nonzero rate computes balance * rate / 1200 into S9(09)V99,\n        without ROUNDED, adds the result to the account accumulator and writes\n        a transaction, including when the computed amount is zero or negative.\n        No fees are computed; the fee paragraph is unimplemented.\n\n        Generated ID is the ten-character parameter followed by a six-digit\n        counter, initially 000001, incremented only for generated transactions.\n        The parameter is not parsed as a date, and PARM-LENGTH is not checked.\n        Counter overflow has no explicit handling. Type is \"01\", numeric category\n        is 0005, source is \"System\", description starts with \"Int. for a/c \"\n        followed by the eleven-digit account ID. Merchant ID is zero and merchant\n        name, city and ZIP are spaces. Card number comes from the alternate-key\n        cross reference. Both timestamps use CURRENT-DATE independently of\n        the supplied ID prefix, in YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 form.\n\n        The final account is NOT explicitly flushed after the loop. The apparent\n        EOF update is an ELSE inside a loop tested UNTIL END-OF-FILE = 'Y';\n        once the read sets EOF, that ELSE is not reached. Thus normal execution\n        updates accounts only when a later account is encountered; the last\n        account retains its previous persistent balance and cycle amounts.\n        A single-account input can generate transactions without rewriting any\n        account. Empty input produces no transactions or account rewrites.\n\n        Category balances are not changed. Generated transactions are not posted\n        through CBTRN02C and are not automatically merged into the transaction\n        master. COMBTRAN is separate infrastructure, not an effect of this call.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Category balances must be available as an indexed file with sequential key access.\n        - The cross-reference binding must support the declared account-ID alternate key.\n        - Account and disclosure files must support random keyed reads; account rewrites require I-O access.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Selection among multiple cards for one account is not resolved by the supplied alternate-key declaration and JCL.\n        - TRAN-RECORD is not initialized before each generated write; description tail and filler are not explicitly set.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [idPrefix, categoryBalanceFile, crossReferenceFile, accountFile, disclosureGroupFile]\n              properties:\n                idPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: Exact PARM-DATE PIC X(10); arbitrary characters, including spaces, are representable.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                disclosureGroupFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed interest pass; generated records do not imply final-account persistence.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions, diagnostics]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: TRANSACT sequential output in generated order.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Observed runtime return code; the source does not explicitly assign one on normal completion.\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/AbnormalExecution'\n  /transaction-reports:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce the fixed-width transaction detail report\n      description: |\n        Runs CBTRN03C on a supplied sequential transaction stream. Opens TRANFILE,\n        CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, TRANCATG and DATEPARM INPUT, and TRANREPT OUTPUT.\n        Only the first DATEPARM record is read: positions 1-10 are startDate,\n        position 11 is ignored, and positions 12-21 are endDate. Remaining\n        characters and subsequent records are unused. Empty DATEPARM sets EOF\n        before transaction processing and yields an empty report. Dates are\n        unvalidated character values; reversed or non-calendar ranges remain\n        representable.\n\n        Selection compares the first ten characters of processingTimestamp\n        inclusively to the start and end values as COBOL character fields.\n        Out-of-range input executes NEXT SENTENCE, skipping the remainder of\n        that iteration. The operation performs no sorting and no master unload.\n        CARDXREF is looked up on each selected card-number change; type and\n        type/category descriptions are looked up for each selected record.\n        INVALID KEY in any of these lookups displays the invalid key, reports\n        status 23 and calls the abnormal-termination paragraph. Other lookup\n        statuses are not generally checked.\n\n        Output records are 133 characters. Initial headings identify DALYREPT,\n        Daily Transaction Report and the date range. Detail fields are\n        transaction ID, cross-reference account ID, type, first 15 characters\n        of type description, category, first 29 characters of category\n        description, source and amount edited as -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ.\n        Totals use +ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ with Page Total, Account Total or Grand Total\n        labels and dot leaders. Shorter copybook groups are space-padded.\n\n        \"Account Total\" is a subtotal of consecutive selected card-number\n        groups, not a regrouping by account ID. Unsorted input is accepted and\n        can yield multiple subtotals for the same card or account. It is written\n        on a selected card change, not explicitly for the final card.\n\n        Page size is a line-counter modulus of 20 checked before each detail,\n        not twenty details per page. Headers add four lines; page and account\n        totals each add two including a dashed line. Page totals accumulate\n        into the grand total and reset the page accumulator.\n\n        The date test occurs even after transaction EOF. If the retained record\n        passes the range test, the EOF branch adds its amount again to page\n        and account totals, writes page totals and then grand totals, without a\n        final account subtotal. If the retained record fails the range test,\n        NEXT SENTENCE skips that finalization. Empty transaction input depends\n        on unspecified initial TRAN-RECORD contents. This contract preserves\n        emitted report lines rather than substituting corrected aggregates.\n        No account, balance or transaction master is modified.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Contents retained after an unsuccessful read, including empty-input behavior, depend on the runtime; final totals are not guaranteed to equal the detail sum.\n        - The JCL SORT treats card numbers as zoned decimal, while the program treats them as PIC X(16). This operation does not impose numeric card validation.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameters, crossReferenceFile, transactionTypeFile, transactionCategoryFile]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Exact sequential order presented to CBTRN03C; empty and unsorted streams are allowed.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                dateParameters:\n                  type: array\n                  description: DATEPARM stream; only the first record is read. No minimum record count.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    minLength: 80\n                    maxLength: 80\n                    description: An exact 80-character DATEPARM record, including ignored characters.\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionTypeFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionCategoryFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed report generation; output includes source control-flow and formatting behavior.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [lines, diagnostics]\n                properties:\n                  lines:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportLines'\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Observed runtime code, not explicitly assigned on normal completion.\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/AbnormalExecution'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    AbnormalExecution:\n      description: |\n        Runtime failure or source abnormal-termination path. Checked nonzero\n        OPEN/CLOSE statuses, unexpected sequential READ statuses, and checked\n        WRITE/REWRITE failures display diagnostics and call CEE3ABD with code\n        999 and timing 0. Sequential status 10 is normal EOF. Posting category\n        reads and primary disclosure reads also accept 23 as described by their\n        operations. Missing report references and missing interest account,\n        cross reference or default disclosure can reach this response.\n        No output cleanup or rollback is established. Failure of the external\n        termination service itself is environment-dependent.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  schemas:\n    DatasetBinding:\n      type: string\n      description: |\n        Opaque transport identifier for an externally provisioned persistent\n        dataset. No existence or referential-integrity constraint is imposed by\n        this schema. Resolution must preserve the program's file mode, key and\n        failure behavior; it must not silently substitute an empty dataset.\n    Amount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,9}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(09)V99 decimal, including zero and negative amounts; maximum absolute value 999999999.99.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,10}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(10)V99 decimal; maximum absolute value 9999999999.99.\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'\n    Timestamp:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: |\n        PIC X(26), not an RFC 3339 timestamp. Arbitrary character content is\n        representable. Input is space-padded, not calendar-validated. Generated\n        values use YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 from CURRENT-DATE.\n    TransactionInput:\n      oneOf:\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n    RawTransaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [recordBase64]\n      properties:\n        recordBase64:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          description: |\n            Exactly 350 decoded bytes in the runtime's record encoding, without\n            sequential-file framing. Layout is CVTRA05Y/CVTRA06Y. This form\n            preserves arbitrary PIC X contents, filler, signs and malformed\n            numeric bytes. Byte length is a transport representation rule, not\n            a business validation; malformed numeric content has no specified\n            business rejection and may cause runtime failure.\n          x-decoded-byte-length: 350\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required:\n        - id\n        - typeCode\n        - categoryCode\n        - source\n        - description\n        - amount\n        - merchantId\n        - merchantName\n        - merchantCity\n        - merchantZip\n        - cardNumber\n        - originalTimestamp\n        - processingTimestamp\n        - filler\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16) indexed posting key; blank and duplicate values are not excluded.\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n          description: PIC X(02); no enumeration is imposed.\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16), not restricted to digits or a card-number checksum.\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n          description: Preserved on rejection; not explicitly moved into a posted or generated record.\n    PostingResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [processedCount, rejectedCount, transactions, rejects, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        processedCount:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n          description: Successfully read daily records, including rejects; PIC 9(09).\n        rejectedCount:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n        returnCode:\n          type: integer\n          description: Observed COBOL RETURN-CODE; explicitly 4 if rejectedCount is positive.\n        transactions:\n          type: array\n          description: Successfully written TRANFILE records from this invocation, not a merged historical master.\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        rejects:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingReject'\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    PostingReject:\n      type: object\n      required: [inputRecord, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        inputRecord:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          enum:\n            - INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\n            - ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\n            - OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\n            - TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\n          description: Transport removes trailing padding; physical trailer pads this to 76 characters.\n      description: |\n        DALYREJS physical record is 430 bytes: unchanged input 350, reason 4,\n        description 76. Reason 0109 is an internal posting-rewrite flag and\n        does not enter this stream.\n    ReportLines:\n      type: array\n      items:\n        type: string\n        minLength: 133\n        maxLength: 133\n      description: TRANREPT records in write order, with trailing spaces retained and no inserted page breaks.\n    Diagnostics:\n      type: array\n      items:\n        type: string\n      description: |\n        Observed DISPLAY output in order, including execution markers, input\n        displays, posting counts and file-status diagnostics when emitted.\n        A displayed status may use the source's four-character conversion of\n        two-byte file status. Posting reject-file close errors mistakenly move\n        XREFFILE status to the diagnostic field; no correction is promised.\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      type: object\n      required: [program, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        program:\n          type: string\n          enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        phase:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed failing paragraph or I/O action, if available.\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed status representation, if available; not necessarily a business reason.\n        requestedAbendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present only when the source abnormal-termination call is observed.\n        partialTransactions:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        partialRejects:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingReject'\n        partialReportLines:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportLines'\n      description: |\n        Partial artifact properties are present only when retrievable. Their\n        absence does not establish that no writes or persistent effects occurred.\n    AccountState:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        Logical view of externally provisioned CVACT01Y records, 300 bytes,\n        keyed by accountId. This schema documents dependency state, not an\n        account maintenance API. Unmentioned fields survive successful rewrites.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n          description: Not checked by these programs.\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n          description: ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE; compared lexically, not parsed.\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        currentCycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        currentCycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CrossReferenceState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT03Y, 50 bytes; primary card key, with account alternate key required by interest generation.\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalanceState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA01Y, 50 bytes; composite key is accountId, typeCode, categoryCode in that order.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureGroupState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA02Y, 50 bytes; composite key is groupId, typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        interestRate:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,4}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n          description: S9(04)V99; signed annual percentage divided by 1200 in monthly calculation.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionTypeState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA03Y, 60 bytes; keyed by typeCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategoryState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA04Y, 60 bytes; composite key is typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\nx-dependency-layouts:\n  ACCTFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountState'\n  XREFFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReferenceState'\n  CARDXREF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReferenceState'\n  TCATBALF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalanceState'\n  DISCGRP:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/DisclosureGroupState'\n  TRANTYPE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionTypeState'\n  TRANCATG:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionCategoryState'\n  TRANFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n    description: Indexed OUTPUT for posting; sequential INPUT for reporting. Conversion between these is not implicit.\n"}

event: response.content_part.done
data: {"type":"response.content_part.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_08b2f514691c0c8f016aa3e5c73f7487d28f1581baff4e63f2","output_index":1,"part":{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Transaction Batch Boundary\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract derived from CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C, their supplied\n    copybooks and batch dependencies. The three operations invoke individual\n    program capabilities, not the complete JCL schedule.\n\n    HTTP POST, JSON envelopes, dataset binding identifiers, inline sequential\n    records and returned artifacts are chosen transport conventions. They are\n    not interfaces implemented by the COBOL source. A dataset binding identifies\n    an environment-provisioned file with the specified organization, keys and\n    access permissions; it does not create, validate, back up or repair that file.\n    Missing records and unavailable bindings remain representable failure inputs.\n\n    Structured character fields are right-padded with spaces to their PIC X\n    widths. Numeric identifier strings retain leading zeros. Decimal strings\n    encode signed fixed-point values, not floating-point numbers. Raw records\n    provide a lossless alternative, including filler and invalid numeric storage.\n    Raw record encoding and signed DISPLAY representation depend on the bound\n    COBOL runtime. No calendar, card-number, positive-amount, active-account or\n    reference-code validation is added by this contract.\n\n    Program completion, business rejection and abnormal termination are distinct.\n    HTTP 200 denotes a completed invocation, including posting with rejects.\n    HTTP 500 denotes an observed runtime failure or requested abnormal termination,\n    not a transactional rollback. No atomicity, retry, idempotency or automatic\n    recovery is promised. Artifacts and persistent changes may precede failure.\n  license:\n    name: Apache License 2.0\n    identifier: Apache-2.0\nx-uncertainties:\n  - |\n    The supplied JCL references SORT, IDCAMS and CEE3ABD; their implementations\n    and execution in the target environment are not established. REPROC also\n    references CNTLLIB(REPROCT), whose contents are not supplied.\n  - |\n    TRANBKP describes unloading, deleting and redefining the transaction master.\n    COMBTRAN describes sorting a backup plus system transactions by transaction\n    ID and loading the master. Neither is performed implicitly by these operations.\n  - |\n    TRANREPT JCL describes unloading, date filtering and sorting by card number\n    before CBTRN03C. The program operation does not assume those steps run.\n    Its SORT dates are separate from DATEPARM and its JCL has duplicate STEP05R\n    names. No schedule validity or equivalence of date sources is guaranteed.\n  - |\n    Numeric overflow has no explicit ON SIZE ERROR handling. Several working\n    totals use S9(09)V99 even though account balances use S9(10)V99. Runtime\n    behavior for overflow, invalid numeric bytes and unspecified initial storage\n    is not normalized by this contract.\npaths:\n  /transaction-postings:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Post an ordered daily transaction stream\n      description: |\n        Runs CBTRN02C. Opens DALYTRAN INPUT, TRANFILE OUTPUT (indexed,\n        random access, transaction ID key), XREFFILE INPUT, DALYREJS OUTPUT,\n        ACCTFILE I-O and TCATBALF I-O. The source does not open TRANFILE\n        EXTEND or I-O; this is not an append-to-history guarantee. Provisioning\n        and OPEN OUTPUT behavior of an existing indexed file are runtime\n        preconditions, not a hidden backup/reload workflow.\n\n        Each successfully read daily record increments the processed count.\n        Card lookup precedes account lookup. INVALID KEY on card lookup rejects\n        with 0100, \"INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\". INVALID KEY on account lookup\n        rejects with 0101, \"ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\". For a found account,\n        temporary balance is currentCycleCredit - currentCycleDebit + amount\n        in S9(09)V99. A value greater than creditLimit sets 0102,\n        \"OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\". Then expirationDate is compared as PIC X(10)\n        against the first ten characters of originalTimestamp. An earlier\n        expiration sets 0103, \"TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\",\n        overwriting 0102 if both apply. Equality passes both tests.\n        These lookups do not generally check all file statuses.\n\n        A rejected record writes the unchanged 350-byte input plus a four-digit\n        reason and a space-padded 76-character description. It does not enter\n        posting. Processing continues. A completed run with any rejects explicitly\n        sets COBOL RETURN-CODE to 4; no explicit zero assignment is made for a\n        reject-free run.\n\n        For a validated record, named transaction fields are copied, except\n        processingTimestamp is replaced by CURRENT-DATE in\n        YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 form. Input processingTimestamp is not used\n        for validation or posting. Output filler is not explicitly copied.\n\n        Persistent effects occur in this order:\n        1. Read category balance by account ID, type and category; status 23\n           creates an initialized record with balance equal to amount, otherwise\n           add amount and rewrite.\n        2. Add amount to account currentBalance. For amount >= 0 add amount to\n           currentCycleCredit; for negative amount add the negative amount to\n           currentCycleDebit. Rewrite the account.\n        3. Write the transaction keyed by its supplied ID.\n\n        Account rewrite INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109,\n        \"ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\", but the caller does not revisit rejection,\n        count it as rejected or write a reject record; transaction writing still\n        follows. Other account rewrite statuses are not explicitly checked.\n        Duplicate transaction IDs are not prevalidated or deduplicated. A\n        duplicate-key write failure takes the abnormal path after preceding\n        balance effects. Processing preserves input order; later records can\n        observe earlier changes.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Indexed master files must be provisioned and accessible in the declared modes.\n        - XREFFILE is keyed by card number; ACCTFILE by account ID; TCATBALF by account ID, type and category.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [dailyTransactions, transactionFile, crossReferenceFile, accountFile, categoryBalanceFile]\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  type: array\n                  description: DALYTRAN records in read order; empty input is allowed. IDs need not be unique.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                transactionFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed, possibly with business rejects and COBOL return code 4.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/AbnormalExecution'\n  /interest-transactions:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate sequential system interest transactions from category balances\n      description: |\n        Runs CBACT04C. Opens TCATBALF INPUT for sequential indexed-key traversal,\n        XREFFILE INPUT with account-ID alternate-key lookup, DISCGRP INPUT,\n        ACCTFILE I-O, and TRANSACT OUTPUT as a new sequential artifact.\n\n        On each account change, except the first, rewrite the previous account:\n        add accumulated monthly interest to currentBalance and set both cycle\n        credit and debit to zero. Then reset the accumulated interest, read the\n        new account and read its cross reference by account ID. Missing account\n        or cross reference is abnormal termination, not a skipped account.\n\n        For each category balance, look up disclosure rate by account group,\n        transaction type and category. Status 23 retries the lookup using the\n        space-padded group \"DEFAULT\" and the same type/category. Failure of this\n        default lookup is abnormal termination. A zero rate generates nothing.\n        Every nonzero rate computes balance * rate / 1200 into S9(09)V99,\n        without ROUNDED, adds the result to the account accumulator and writes\n        a transaction, including when the computed amount is zero or negative.\n        No fees are computed; the fee paragraph is unimplemented.\n\n        Generated ID is the ten-character parameter followed by a six-digit\n        counter, initially 000001, incremented only for generated transactions.\n        The parameter is not parsed as a date, and PARM-LENGTH is not checked.\n        Counter overflow has no explicit handling. Type is \"01\", numeric category\n        is 0005, source is \"System\", description starts with \"Int. for a/c \"\n        followed by the eleven-digit account ID. Merchant ID is zero and merchant\n        name, city and ZIP are spaces. Card number comes from the alternate-key\n        cross reference. Both timestamps use CURRENT-DATE independently of\n        the supplied ID prefix, in YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 form.\n\n        The final account is NOT explicitly flushed after the loop. The apparent\n        EOF update is an ELSE inside a loop tested UNTIL END-OF-FILE = 'Y';\n        once the read sets EOF, that ELSE is not reached. Thus normal execution\n        updates accounts only when a later account is encountered; the last\n        account retains its previous persistent balance and cycle amounts.\n        A single-account input can generate transactions without rewriting any\n        account. Empty input produces no transactions or account rewrites.\n\n        Category balances are not changed. Generated transactions are not posted\n        through CBTRN02C and are not automatically merged into the transaction\n        master. COMBTRAN is separate infrastructure, not an effect of this call.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Category balances must be available as an indexed file with sequential key access.\n        - The cross-reference binding must support the declared account-ID alternate key.\n        - Account and disclosure files must support random keyed reads; account rewrites require I-O access.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Selection among multiple cards for one account is not resolved by the supplied alternate-key declaration and JCL.\n        - TRAN-RECORD is not initialized before each generated write; description tail and filler are not explicitly set.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [idPrefix, categoryBalanceFile, crossReferenceFile, accountFile, disclosureGroupFile]\n              properties:\n                idPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: Exact PARM-DATE PIC X(10); arbitrary characters, including spaces, are representable.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                disclosureGroupFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed interest pass; generated records do not imply final-account persistence.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions, diagnostics]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: TRANSACT sequential output in generated order.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Observed runtime return code; the source does not explicitly assign one on normal completion.\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/AbnormalExecution'\n  /transaction-reports:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce the fixed-width transaction detail report\n      description: |\n        Runs CBTRN03C on a supplied sequential transaction stream. Opens TRANFILE,\n        CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, TRANCATG and DATEPARM INPUT, and TRANREPT OUTPUT.\n        Only the first DATEPARM record is read: positions 1-10 are startDate,\n        position 11 is ignored, and positions 12-21 are endDate. Remaining\n        characters and subsequent records are unused. Empty DATEPARM sets EOF\n        before transaction processing and yields an empty report. Dates are\n        unvalidated character values; reversed or non-calendar ranges remain\n        representable.\n\n        Selection compares the first ten characters of processingTimestamp\n        inclusively to the start and end values as COBOL character fields.\n        Out-of-range input executes NEXT SENTENCE, skipping the remainder of\n        that iteration. The operation performs no sorting and no master unload.\n        CARDXREF is looked up on each selected card-number change; type and\n        type/category descriptions are looked up for each selected record.\n        INVALID KEY in any of these lookups displays the invalid key, reports\n        status 23 and calls the abnormal-termination paragraph. Other lookup\n        statuses are not generally checked.\n\n        Output records are 133 characters. Initial headings identify DALYREPT,\n        Daily Transaction Report and the date range. Detail fields are\n        transaction ID, cross-reference account ID, type, first 15 characters\n        of type description, category, first 29 characters of category\n        description, source and amount edited as -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ.\n        Totals use +ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ with Page Total, Account Total or Grand Total\n        labels and dot leaders. Shorter copybook groups are space-padded.\n\n        \"Account Total\" is a subtotal of consecutive selected card-number\n        groups, not a regrouping by account ID. Unsorted input is accepted and\n        can yield multiple subtotals for the same card or account. It is written\n        on a selected card change, not explicitly for the final card.\n\n        Page size is a line-counter modulus of 20 checked before each detail,\n        not twenty details per page. Headers add four lines; page and account\n        totals each add two including a dashed line. Page totals accumulate\n        into the grand total and reset the page accumulator.\n\n        The date test occurs even after transaction EOF. If the retained record\n        passes the range test, the EOF branch adds its amount again to page\n        and account totals, writes page totals and then grand totals, without a\n        final account subtotal. If the retained record fails the range test,\n        NEXT SENTENCE skips that finalization. Empty transaction input depends\n        on unspecified initial TRAN-RECORD contents. This contract preserves\n        emitted report lines rather than substituting corrected aggregates.\n        No account, balance or transaction master is modified.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Contents retained after an unsuccessful read, including empty-input behavior, depend on the runtime; final totals are not guaranteed to equal the detail sum.\n        - The JCL SORT treats card numbers as zoned decimal, while the program treats them as PIC X(16). This operation does not impose numeric card validation.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameters, crossReferenceFile, transactionTypeFile, transactionCategoryFile]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Exact sequential order presented to CBTRN03C; empty and unsorted streams are allowed.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                dateParameters:\n                  type: array\n                  description: DATEPARM stream; only the first record is read. No minimum record count.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    minLength: 80\n                    maxLength: 80\n                    description: An exact 80-character DATEPARM record, including ignored characters.\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionTypeFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionCategoryFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed report generation; output includes source control-flow and formatting behavior.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [lines, diagnostics]\n                properties:\n                  lines:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportLines'\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Observed runtime code, not explicitly assigned on normal completion.\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/AbnormalExecution'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    AbnormalExecution:\n      description: |\n        Runtime failure or source abnormal-termination path. Checked nonzero\n        OPEN/CLOSE statuses, unexpected sequential READ statuses, and checked\n        WRITE/REWRITE failures display diagnostics and call CEE3ABD with code\n        999 and timing 0. Sequential status 10 is normal EOF. Posting category\n        reads and primary disclosure reads also accept 23 as described by their\n        operations. Missing report references and missing interest account,\n        cross reference or default disclosure can reach this response.\n        No output cleanup or rollback is established. Failure of the external\n        termination service itself is environment-dependent.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  schemas:\n    DatasetBinding:\n      type: string\n      description: |\n        Opaque transport identifier for an externally provisioned persistent\n        dataset. No existence or referential-integrity constraint is imposed by\n        this schema. Resolution must preserve the program's file mode, key and\n        failure behavior; it must not silently substitute an empty dataset.\n    Amount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,9}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(09)V99 decimal, including zero and negative amounts; maximum absolute value 999999999.99.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,10}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(10)V99 decimal; maximum absolute value 9999999999.99.\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'\n    Timestamp:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: |\n        PIC X(26), not an RFC 3339 timestamp. Arbitrary character content is\n        representable. Input is space-padded, not calendar-validated. Generated\n        values use YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 from CURRENT-DATE.\n    TransactionInput:\n      oneOf:\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n    RawTransaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [recordBase64]\n      properties:\n        recordBase64:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          description: |\n            Exactly 350 decoded bytes in the runtime's record encoding, without\n            sequential-file framing. Layout is CVTRA05Y/CVTRA06Y. This form\n            preserves arbitrary PIC X contents, filler, signs and malformed\n            numeric bytes. Byte length is a transport representation rule, not\n            a business validation; malformed numeric content has no specified\n            business rejection and may cause runtime failure.\n          x-decoded-byte-length: 350\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required:\n        - id\n        - typeCode\n        - categoryCode\n        - source\n        - description\n        - amount\n        - merchantId\n        - merchantName\n        - merchantCity\n        - merchantZip\n        - cardNumber\n        - originalTimestamp\n        - processingTimestamp\n        - filler\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16) indexed posting key; blank and duplicate values are not excluded.\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n          description: PIC X(02); no enumeration is imposed.\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16), not restricted to digits or a card-number checksum.\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n          description: Preserved on rejection; not explicitly moved into a posted or generated record.\n    PostingResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [processedCount, rejectedCount, transactions, rejects, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        processedCount:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n          description: Successfully read daily records, including rejects; PIC 9(09).\n        rejectedCount:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n        returnCode:\n          type: integer\n          description: Observed COBOL RETURN-CODE; explicitly 4 if rejectedCount is positive.\n        transactions:\n          type: array\n          description: Successfully written TRANFILE records from this invocation, not a merged historical master.\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        rejects:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingReject'\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    PostingReject:\n      type: object\n      required: [inputRecord, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        inputRecord:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          enum:\n            - INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\n            - ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\n            - OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\n            - TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\n          description: Transport removes trailing padding; physical trailer pads this to 76 characters.\n      description: |\n        DALYREJS physical record is 430 bytes: unchanged input 350, reason 4,\n        description 76. Reason 0109 is an internal posting-rewrite flag and\n        does not enter this stream.\n    ReportLines:\n      type: array\n      items:\n        type: string\n        minLength: 133\n        maxLength: 133\n      description: TRANREPT records in write order, with trailing spaces retained and no inserted page breaks.\n    Diagnostics:\n      type: array\n      items:\n        type: string\n      description: |\n        Observed DISPLAY output in order, including execution markers, input\n        displays, posting counts and file-status diagnostics when emitted.\n        A displayed status may use the source's four-character conversion of\n        two-byte file status. Posting reject-file close errors mistakenly move\n        XREFFILE status to the diagnostic field; no correction is promised.\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      type: object\n      required: [program, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        program:\n          type: string\n          enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        phase:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed failing paragraph or I/O action, if available.\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed status representation, if available; not necessarily a business reason.\n        requestedAbendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present only when the source abnormal-termination call is observed.\n        partialTransactions:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        partialRejects:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingReject'\n        partialReportLines:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportLines'\n      description: |\n        Partial artifact properties are present only when retrievable. Their\n        absence does not establish that no writes or persistent effects occurred.\n    AccountState:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        Logical view of externally provisioned CVACT01Y records, 300 bytes,\n        keyed by accountId. This schema documents dependency state, not an\n        account maintenance API. Unmentioned fields survive successful rewrites.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n          description: Not checked by these programs.\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n          description: ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE; compared lexically, not parsed.\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        currentCycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        currentCycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CrossReferenceState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT03Y, 50 bytes; primary card key, with account alternate key required by interest generation.\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalanceState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA01Y, 50 bytes; composite key is accountId, typeCode, categoryCode in that order.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureGroupState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA02Y, 50 bytes; composite key is groupId, typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        interestRate:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,4}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n          description: S9(04)V99; signed annual percentage divided by 1200 in monthly calculation.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionTypeState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA03Y, 60 bytes; keyed by typeCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategoryState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA04Y, 60 bytes; composite key is typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\nx-dependency-layouts:\n  ACCTFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountState'\n  XREFFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReferenceState'\n  CARDXREF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReferenceState'\n  TCATBALF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalanceState'\n  DISCGRP:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/DisclosureGroupState'\n  TRANTYPE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionTypeState'\n  TRANCATG:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionCategoryState'\n  TRANFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n    description: Indexed OUTPUT for posting; sequential INPUT for reporting. Conversion between these is not implicit.\n"},"sequence_number":6459}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"id":"msg_08b2f514691c0c8f016aa3e5c73f7487d28f1581baff4e63f2","type":"message","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Transaction Batch Boundary\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract derived from CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C, their supplied\n    copybooks and batch dependencies. The three operations invoke individual\n    program capabilities, not the complete JCL schedule.\n\n    HTTP POST, JSON envelopes, dataset binding identifiers, inline sequential\n    records and returned artifacts are chosen transport conventions. They are\n    not interfaces implemented by the COBOL source. A dataset binding identifies\n    an environment-provisioned file with the specified organization, keys and\n    access permissions; it does not create, validate, back up or repair that file.\n    Missing records and unavailable bindings remain representable failure inputs.\n\n    Structured character fields are right-padded with spaces to their PIC X\n    widths. Numeric identifier strings retain leading zeros. Decimal strings\n    encode signed fixed-point values, not floating-point numbers. Raw records\n    provide a lossless alternative, including filler and invalid numeric storage.\n    Raw record encoding and signed DISPLAY representation depend on the bound\n    COBOL runtime. No calendar, card-number, positive-amount, active-account or\n    reference-code validation is added by this contract.\n\n    Program completion, business rejection and abnormal termination are distinct.\n    HTTP 200 denotes a completed invocation, including posting with rejects.\n    HTTP 500 denotes an observed runtime failure or requested abnormal termination,\n    not a transactional rollback. No atomicity, retry, idempotency or automatic\n    recovery is promised. Artifacts and persistent changes may precede failure.\n  license:\n    name: Apache License 2.0\n    identifier: Apache-2.0\nx-uncertainties:\n  - |\n    The supplied JCL references SORT, IDCAMS and CEE3ABD; their implementations\n    and execution in the target environment are not established. REPROC also\n    references CNTLLIB(REPROCT), whose contents are not supplied.\n  - |\n    TRANBKP describes unloading, deleting and redefining the transaction master.\n    COMBTRAN describes sorting a backup plus system transactions by transaction\n    ID and loading the master. Neither is performed implicitly by these operations.\n  - |\n    TRANREPT JCL describes unloading, date filtering and sorting by card number\n    before CBTRN03C. The program operation does not assume those steps run.\n    Its SORT dates are separate from DATEPARM and its JCL has duplicate STEP05R\n    names. No schedule validity or equivalence of date sources is guaranteed.\n  - |\n    Numeric overflow has no explicit ON SIZE ERROR handling. Several working\n    totals use S9(09)V99 even though account balances use S9(10)V99. Runtime\n    behavior for overflow, invalid numeric bytes and unspecified initial storage\n    is not normalized by this contract.\npaths:\n  /transaction-postings:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Post an ordered daily transaction stream\n      description: |\n        Runs CBTRN02C. Opens DALYTRAN INPUT, TRANFILE OUTPUT (indexed,\n        random access, transaction ID key), XREFFILE INPUT, DALYREJS OUTPUT,\n        ACCTFILE I-O and TCATBALF I-O. The source does not open TRANFILE\n        EXTEND or I-O; this is not an append-to-history guarantee. Provisioning\n        and OPEN OUTPUT behavior of an existing indexed file are runtime\n        preconditions, not a hidden backup/reload workflow.\n\n        Each successfully read daily record increments the processed count.\n        Card lookup precedes account lookup. INVALID KEY on card lookup rejects\n        with 0100, \"INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\". INVALID KEY on account lookup\n        rejects with 0101, \"ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\". For a found account,\n        temporary balance is currentCycleCredit - currentCycleDebit + amount\n        in S9(09)V99. A value greater than creditLimit sets 0102,\n        \"OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\". Then expirationDate is compared as PIC X(10)\n        against the first ten characters of originalTimestamp. An earlier\n        expiration sets 0103, \"TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\",\n        overwriting 0102 if both apply. Equality passes both tests.\n        These lookups do not generally check all file statuses.\n\n        A rejected record writes the unchanged 350-byte input plus a four-digit\n        reason and a space-padded 76-character description. It does not enter\n        posting. Processing continues. A completed run with any rejects explicitly\n        sets COBOL RETURN-CODE to 4; no explicit zero assignment is made for a\n        reject-free run.\n\n        For a validated record, named transaction fields are copied, except\n        processingTimestamp is replaced by CURRENT-DATE in\n        YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 form. Input processingTimestamp is not used\n        for validation or posting. Output filler is not explicitly copied.\n\n        Persistent effects occur in this order:\n        1. Read category balance by account ID, type and category; status 23\n           creates an initialized record with balance equal to amount, otherwise\n           add amount and rewrite.\n        2. Add amount to account currentBalance. For amount >= 0 add amount to\n           currentCycleCredit; for negative amount add the negative amount to\n           currentCycleDebit. Rewrite the account.\n        3. Write the transaction keyed by its supplied ID.\n\n        Account rewrite INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109,\n        \"ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\", but the caller does not revisit rejection,\n        count it as rejected or write a reject record; transaction writing still\n        follows. Other account rewrite statuses are not explicitly checked.\n        Duplicate transaction IDs are not prevalidated or deduplicated. A\n        duplicate-key write failure takes the abnormal path after preceding\n        balance effects. Processing preserves input order; later records can\n        observe earlier changes.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Indexed master files must be provisioned and accessible in the declared modes.\n        - XREFFILE is keyed by card number; ACCTFILE by account ID; TCATBALF by account ID, type and category.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [dailyTransactions, transactionFile, crossReferenceFile, accountFile, categoryBalanceFile]\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  type: array\n                  description: DALYTRAN records in read order; empty input is allowed. IDs need not be unique.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                transactionFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed, possibly with business rejects and COBOL return code 4.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/AbnormalExecution'\n  /interest-transactions:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate sequential system interest transactions from category balances\n      description: |\n        Runs CBACT04C. Opens TCATBALF INPUT for sequential indexed-key traversal,\n        XREFFILE INPUT with account-ID alternate-key lookup, DISCGRP INPUT,\n        ACCTFILE I-O, and TRANSACT OUTPUT as a new sequential artifact.\n\n        On each account change, except the first, rewrite the previous account:\n        add accumulated monthly interest to currentBalance and set both cycle\n        credit and debit to zero. Then reset the accumulated interest, read the\n        new account and read its cross reference by account ID. Missing account\n        or cross reference is abnormal termination, not a skipped account.\n\n        For each category balance, look up disclosure rate by account group,\n        transaction type and category. Status 23 retries the lookup using the\n        space-padded group \"DEFAULT\" and the same type/category. Failure of this\n        default lookup is abnormal termination. A zero rate generates nothing.\n        Every nonzero rate computes balance * rate / 1200 into S9(09)V99,\n        without ROUNDED, adds the result to the account accumulator and writes\n        a transaction, including when the computed amount is zero or negative.\n        No fees are computed; the fee paragraph is unimplemented.\n\n        Generated ID is the ten-character parameter followed by a six-digit\n        counter, initially 000001, incremented only for generated transactions.\n        The parameter is not parsed as a date, and PARM-LENGTH is not checked.\n        Counter overflow has no explicit handling. Type is \"01\", numeric category\n        is 0005, source is \"System\", description starts with \"Int. for a/c \"\n        followed by the eleven-digit account ID. Merchant ID is zero and merchant\n        name, city and ZIP are spaces. Card number comes from the alternate-key\n        cross reference. Both timestamps use CURRENT-DATE independently of\n        the supplied ID prefix, in YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 form.\n\n        The final account is NOT explicitly flushed after the loop. The apparent\n        EOF update is an ELSE inside a loop tested UNTIL END-OF-FILE = 'Y';\n        once the read sets EOF, that ELSE is not reached. Thus normal execution\n        updates accounts only when a later account is encountered; the last\n        account retains its previous persistent balance and cycle amounts.\n        A single-account input can generate transactions without rewriting any\n        account. Empty input produces no transactions or account rewrites.\n\n        Category balances are not changed. Generated transactions are not posted\n        through CBTRN02C and are not automatically merged into the transaction\n        master. COMBTRAN is separate infrastructure, not an effect of this call.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Category balances must be available as an indexed file with sequential key access.\n        - The cross-reference binding must support the declared account-ID alternate key.\n        - Account and disclosure files must support random keyed reads; account rewrites require I-O access.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Selection among multiple cards for one account is not resolved by the supplied alternate-key declaration and JCL.\n        - TRAN-RECORD is not initialized before each generated write; description tail and filler are not explicitly set.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [idPrefix, categoryBalanceFile, crossReferenceFile, accountFile, disclosureGroupFile]\n              properties:\n                idPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: Exact PARM-DATE PIC X(10); arbitrary characters, including spaces, are representable.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                disclosureGroupFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed interest pass; generated records do not imply final-account persistence.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions, diagnostics]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: TRANSACT sequential output in generated order.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Observed runtime return code; the source does not explicitly assign one on normal completion.\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/AbnormalExecution'\n  /transaction-reports:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce the fixed-width transaction detail report\n      description: |\n        Runs CBTRN03C on a supplied sequential transaction stream. Opens TRANFILE,\n        CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, TRANCATG and DATEPARM INPUT, and TRANREPT OUTPUT.\n        Only the first DATEPARM record is read: positions 1-10 are startDate,\n        position 11 is ignored, and positions 12-21 are endDate. Remaining\n        characters and subsequent records are unused. Empty DATEPARM sets EOF\n        before transaction processing and yields an empty report. Dates are\n        unvalidated character values; reversed or non-calendar ranges remain\n        representable.\n\n        Selection compares the first ten characters of processingTimestamp\n        inclusively to the start and end values as COBOL character fields.\n        Out-of-range input executes NEXT SENTENCE, skipping the remainder of\n        that iteration. The operation performs no sorting and no master unload.\n        CARDXREF is looked up on each selected card-number change; type and\n        type/category descriptions are looked up for each selected record.\n        INVALID KEY in any of these lookups displays the invalid key, reports\n        status 23 and calls the abnormal-termination paragraph. Other lookup\n        statuses are not generally checked.\n\n        Output records are 133 characters. Initial headings identify DALYREPT,\n        Daily Transaction Report and the date range. Detail fields are\n        transaction ID, cross-reference account ID, type, first 15 characters\n        of type description, category, first 29 characters of category\n        description, source and amount edited as -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ.\n        Totals use +ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ with Page Total, Account Total or Grand Total\n        labels and dot leaders. Shorter copybook groups are space-padded.\n\n        \"Account Total\" is a subtotal of consecutive selected card-number\n        groups, not a regrouping by account ID. Unsorted input is accepted and\n        can yield multiple subtotals for the same card or account. It is written\n        on a selected card change, not explicitly for the final card.\n\n        Page size is a line-counter modulus of 20 checked before each detail,\n        not twenty details per page. Headers add four lines; page and account\n        totals each add two including a dashed line. Page totals accumulate\n        into the grand total and reset the page accumulator.\n\n        The date test occurs even after transaction EOF. If the retained record\n        passes the range test, the EOF branch adds its amount again to page\n        and account totals, writes page totals and then grand totals, without a\n        final account subtotal. If the retained record fails the range test,\n        NEXT SENTENCE skips that finalization. Empty transaction input depends\n        on unspecified initial TRAN-RECORD contents. This contract preserves\n        emitted report lines rather than substituting corrected aggregates.\n        No account, balance or transaction master is modified.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Contents retained after an unsuccessful read, including empty-input behavior, depend on the runtime; final totals are not guaranteed to equal the detail sum.\n        - The JCL SORT treats card numbers as zoned decimal, while the program treats them as PIC X(16). This operation does not impose numeric card validation.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameters, crossReferenceFile, transactionTypeFile, transactionCategoryFile]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Exact sequential order presented to CBTRN03C; empty and unsorted streams are allowed.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                dateParameters:\n                  type: array\n                  description: DATEPARM stream; only the first record is read. No minimum record count.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    minLength: 80\n                    maxLength: 80\n                    description: An exact 80-character DATEPARM record, including ignored characters.\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionTypeFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionCategoryFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed report generation; output includes source control-flow and formatting behavior.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [lines, diagnostics]\n                properties:\n                  lines:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportLines'\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Observed runtime code, not explicitly assigned on normal completion.\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/AbnormalExecution'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    AbnormalExecution:\n      description: |\n        Runtime failure or source abnormal-termination path. Checked nonzero\n        OPEN/CLOSE statuses, unexpected sequential READ statuses, and checked\n        WRITE/REWRITE failures display diagnostics and call CEE3ABD with code\n        999 and timing 0. Sequential status 10 is normal EOF. Posting category\n        reads and primary disclosure reads also accept 23 as described by their\n        operations. Missing report references and missing interest account,\n        cross reference or default disclosure can reach this response.\n        No output cleanup or rollback is established. Failure of the external\n        termination service itself is environment-dependent.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  schemas:\n    DatasetBinding:\n      type: string\n      description: |\n        Opaque transport identifier for an externally provisioned persistent\n        dataset. No existence or referential-integrity constraint is imposed by\n        this schema. Resolution must preserve the program's file mode, key and\n        failure behavior; it must not silently substitute an empty dataset.\n    Amount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,9}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(09)V99 decimal, including zero and negative amounts; maximum absolute value 999999999.99.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,10}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(10)V99 decimal; maximum absolute value 9999999999.99.\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'\n    Timestamp:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: |\n        PIC X(26), not an RFC 3339 timestamp. Arbitrary character content is\n        representable. Input is space-padded, not calendar-validated. Generated\n        values use YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 from CURRENT-DATE.\n    TransactionInput:\n      oneOf:\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n    RawTransaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [recordBase64]\n      properties:\n        recordBase64:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          description: |\n            Exactly 350 decoded bytes in the runtime's record encoding, without\n            sequential-file framing. Layout is CVTRA05Y/CVTRA06Y. This form\n            preserves arbitrary PIC X contents, filler, signs and malformed\n            numeric bytes. Byte length is a transport representation rule, not\n            a business validation; malformed numeric content has no specified\n            business rejection and may cause runtime failure.\n          x-decoded-byte-length: 350\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required:\n        - id\n        - typeCode\n        - categoryCode\n        - source\n        - description\n        - amount\n        - merchantId\n        - merchantName\n        - merchantCity\n        - merchantZip\n        - cardNumber\n        - originalTimestamp\n        - processingTimestamp\n        - filler\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16) indexed posting key; blank and duplicate values are not excluded.\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n          description: PIC X(02); no enumeration is imposed.\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16), not restricted to digits or a card-number checksum.\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n          description: Preserved on rejection; not explicitly moved into a posted or generated record.\n    PostingResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [processedCount, rejectedCount, transactions, rejects, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        processedCount:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n          description: Successfully read daily records, including rejects; PIC 9(09).\n        rejectedCount:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n        returnCode:\n          type: integer\n          description: Observed COBOL RETURN-CODE; explicitly 4 if rejectedCount is positive.\n        transactions:\n          type: array\n          description: Successfully written TRANFILE records from this invocation, not a merged historical master.\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        rejects:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingReject'\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    PostingReject:\n      type: object\n      required: [inputRecord, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        inputRecord:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          enum:\n            - INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\n            - ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\n            - OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\n            - TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\n          description: Transport removes trailing padding; physical trailer pads this to 76 characters.\n      description: |\n        DALYREJS physical record is 430 bytes: unchanged input 350, reason 4,\n        description 76. Reason 0109 is an internal posting-rewrite flag and\n        does not enter this stream.\n    ReportLines:\n      type: array\n      items:\n        type: string\n        minLength: 133\n        maxLength: 133\n      description: TRANREPT records in write order, with trailing spaces retained and no inserted page breaks.\n    Diagnostics:\n      type: array\n      items:\n        type: string\n      description: |\n        Observed DISPLAY output in order, including execution markers, input\n        displays, posting counts and file-status diagnostics when emitted.\n        A displayed status may use the source's four-character conversion of\n        two-byte file status. Posting reject-file close errors mistakenly move\n        XREFFILE status to the diagnostic field; no correction is promised.\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      type: object\n      required: [program, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        program:\n          type: string\n          enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        phase:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed failing paragraph or I/O action, if available.\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed status representation, if available; not necessarily a business reason.\n        requestedAbendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present only when the source abnormal-termination call is observed.\n        partialTransactions:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        partialRejects:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingReject'\n        partialReportLines:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportLines'\n      description: |\n        Partial artifact properties are present only when retrievable. Their\n        absence does not establish that no writes or persistent effects occurred.\n    AccountState:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        Logical view of externally provisioned CVACT01Y records, 300 bytes,\n        keyed by accountId. This schema documents dependency state, not an\n        account maintenance API. Unmentioned fields survive successful rewrites.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n          description: Not checked by these programs.\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n          description: ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE; compared lexically, not parsed.\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        currentCycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        currentCycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CrossReferenceState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT03Y, 50 bytes; primary card key, with account alternate key required by interest generation.\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalanceState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA01Y, 50 bytes; composite key is accountId, typeCode, categoryCode in that order.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureGroupState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA02Y, 50 bytes; composite key is groupId, typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        interestRate:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,4}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n          description: S9(04)V99; signed annual percentage divided by 1200 in monthly calculation.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionTypeState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA03Y, 60 bytes; keyed by typeCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategoryState:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA04Y, 60 bytes; composite key is typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 2\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\nx-dependency-layouts:\n  ACCTFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountState'\n  XREFFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReferenceState'\n  CARDXREF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReferenceState'\n  TCATBALF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalanceState'\n  DISCGRP:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/DisclosureGroupState'\n  TRANTYPE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionTypeState'\n  TRANCATG:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionCategoryState'\n  TRANFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n    description: Indexed OUTPUT for posting; sequential INPUT for reporting. Conversion between these is not implicit.\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"},"output_index":1,"sequence_number":6460}

